{"id":1828903,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-18T19:30:35.723Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/vPt6wNHBUDJrP7uZOTtoWuwUKo4.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":99,"name":"Documentary"}],"homepage":"","id":1828903,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["FR"],"original_language":"fr","original_title":"L'éternel de Takada","overview":"The Mondial is the oldest movie theater in Japan still in operation. It was built in 1911, in northern Japan, in Takada, then a garrison town. In the 1960s, the military abandoned it. Only the heart of the small town, made up of traditional wooden houses, remained. The outskirts became a ghost town. Threatened with bankruptcy, the Mondial was saved for the first time by Studio Nikkatsu, a producer of erotic films. At the end of the 1970s, the Mondial, a victim of an earthquake, would have been permanently destroyed if a man—Mr. Masumura—a monk, film buff, and jazz lover, and a few friends had not fought to save it and organize a film club there. The members are now his age, in their 70s, and one of the members is over 90, but the fervor remains intact. This is all the more true as the film club is preparing a new screening to celebrate the end of winter.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/3SlP4KqFi839AOAnREZHmexpfp3.jpg","production_companies":[{"id":112963,"logo_path":"/ccSxSr2Kgdt6jzAjHHvDn8K3xKD.png","name":"Kolam Productions","origin_country":"FR"}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"FR","name":"France"}],"release_date":"2026-11-29","revenue":0,"runtime":52,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"Japanese","iso_639_1":"ja","name":"日本語"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"The Eternal of Takada","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":6677343,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Shun-ichi Masumura","original_name":"Shun-ichi Masumura","popularity":0,"profile_path":null,"cast_id":9,"character":"Self",